Cell["\<\
A compiler restricted to fewer independent motions than 3 is flagged as \
intensity-emulable no matter what its click statistics say \[LongDash] which \
is exactly the audit that catches the tuned cheater of Stage 4. This is gate \
G7, and it belongs to Category 3 for an honest reason: its input is a \
declaration about the claimed dynamics, a white-box element, not a black-box \
observable. It certifies that a claimed mechanism is or is not \
classically-optically compilable; it does not read the twist off the clicks. \
Two lenses, not one, is the price of certainty here. A separate result \
(LP-002) shows the two lenses genuinely answer different questions \
\[LongDash] their values decorrelate under composition \[LongDash] which is \
why neither can be dropped.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0d0cc51c-7d9f-e048-a8a9-4e2e68f85c91"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Stage 6 \[LongDash] The Construct/Certify Loop: the Optical Constructor\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"efa2c9d1-c9b9-b047-ac1d-cf820dc73e36"],

Cell["\<\
Figure strip (Stage 6). Four blueprints the optical constructor actually \
emits, each self-certified (VerifyBlueprint returns OK) before export \
(optical-synthesis):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0cd7446e-b964-794a-bcb7-69109041db13"],

Cell["\<\
Import[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"optical-synthesis\", \
\"schematics\", \"demo1_kcbs_pentagon_L1.png\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"384b4ef5-0d21-254d-b85a-345064cc22ba"],

Cell["\<\
Import[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"optical-synthesis\", \
\"schematics\", \"demo2_c7_heptagon_L1.png\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5ee79db1-509e-6a42-b361-3cecdc6b03cd"],

Cell["\<\
Import[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"optical-synthesis\", \
\"schematics\", \"demo3_cct_mesh_reps2.png\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0c9d1eff-3040-ce43-a775-850322327add"],

Cell["\<\
Import[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"optical-synthesis\", \
\"schematics\", \"demo4_table_V0977_L2.png\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c7f7c8c8-b30f-f04d-9432-76e4f65bcead"],

Cell["\<\
Left to right: the Lapkiewicz KCBS pentagon as a Layer-1 Givens / \
beamsplitter cascade (cos(theta) = 1/GoldenRatio, genuine, so(3) DLA = 3); \
the C7 heptagon Layer-1 cascade (identity S = 7 - 4 \[Theta](C7)); the cct \
pentagon-mesh chain at reps = 2 (18 modes, block-local routing); and a pure \
no-disturbance table at V = 977/1000 realized Layer-2-only (leaf-confined, \
divided-beam intensity schedule).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ab2bc341-d9b9-fa41-a4d2-4e7674741949"],

Cell["\<\
To be sure the two checks actually work, the project also built a constructor \
\[LongDash] the synthesis dual of the test [EMU]. Given a target behaviour it \
emits an actual optical blueprint: either a genuine particle-based device or \
a classical light-splitting fake, with exact numbers, so both checks can be \
run against known, deliberately constructed cases including the Stage-4 \
cheater tuned to fool you. The KCBS pentagon comes out as the Lapkiewicz \
interference cascade, and its one design constant is the golden ratio.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"82ad660d-923c-0041-9a85-013f2bad2eda"],

